A||N||14||polomeno||HELP ! , I installed new clutch pedal.. wont start||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||11-05-2000||06:31 PM||||Hey guys.. last week i started to install a new clutch pedal.. it is not finished and the car just does not start at all.. it's as if the battery is dead when i go to start it.. the starter and battery are both only about 2 weeks old?? any idea's what could cause this or be killin my battery??<P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ronnie||11-05-2000||06:42 PM||||Correct me if I'm wrong , but the clutch has a safety switch on it that only allows the starter to operate if the clutch is engaged.If you cannot operate the clutch , then it can not start.||||reg||1
Z||000002||polomeno||11-05-2000||06:48 PM||||Yep.. there was a saftey switch and i did reattach it, that's what i thought it might be , but it seems to be working fine...??||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||11-05-2000||11:41 PM||||If you turn the key, and the temp guage (I think thats the one) swings but nothing else, it is the safety switch. I couldn't figure out what was wrong with mine.. I attached it to the pedal, and double checked it. Then I had a brainstorm, went under the car, and realized I hadn't connected the actual wires (there is a plug I disconnected and I forgot to plug it back in) Hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000004||polomeno||11-06-2000||12:33 AM||||I just checked and it is the temp gauge that goes and nothing else.. but i never unplugged any wires from under the car?? the only thing i did to the saftey was that platic piece that plugs into side of pedal and i put that back in ..?? I double checked and it all seems to be hooked up.. where is this other wire located?? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||JetroGT||11-06-2000||04:28 AM||||Their is a piece of plastic that slides on a plastic shaft. If it has slid down too far the switch will not work. Just reset it and it should work. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||polomeno||11-06-2000||04:31 AM||||do you mean slide it away from the drivers seat or slide it towards driver seat.. cause when i push clutch down it automaticlly makes a "clicking" sound and pushes itself all the way to the top toward the drivers seat direction?  is this correct?<P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000007||JetroGT||11-06-2000||04:42 AM||||This is what I'm talking about.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Switch.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||JetroGT||11-06-2000||04:45 AM||||I think you should slide it down near the base of the switch.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||polomeno||11-06-2000||04:45 AM||||Yep.. but when you says "slide down too far it wont start" do you mean slide right in your picture or slide left? cuase when i push the pedal down it forces that thing all the way to the left ( in your pic ) <BR>is it too loose or some thing?<P><BR>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000010||JohnnyK||11-06-2000||01:38 PM||||Then try this. Take the actual white plunger thing (that connects to the clutch pedal) with your hand and push it all the way in (towards the front of the car, as if your hand is the pedal) and then try to start. If it does, it's not hooked up to the pedal correctly, if it doesn't it's not hooked up period. Mine is attached the clutch pedal with an aligator clip..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Phil||11-07-2000||10:53 AM||||Or just TEMPORARILY connect the two wires together and see if it starts. If it starts then you know it's the switch.||||reg||1
Z||000012||polomeno||11-07-2000||03:18 PM||||Ok i just tried to jump the 2 wires together and it still does the same thing.. this problem only started after i changed the clutch pedal so i'm pretty sure it must be that switch??  the starter and battery are both brand new.. when i go to start i get no power and the temp gauge goes nuts.. any suggestions please?<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000013||JohnnyK||11-07-2000||04:37 PM||||If the temp guage goes nuts, and you just replaced the pedal, and it only started after that, i'm 99.9% sure it's the neutral safety switch, somewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000014||polomeno||11-07-2000||05:09 PM||||Yes.. i totally agree.. but where else can i check?  i placed a copper wire between the connecters on teh switch to jump them and still nothing.. ?  the switch seems to be working fine and is connected to the pedal fine.. nothing... any idea where else i can look? or do?<P>thanks again<P>John||||reg||1
